{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task AGENT-TF-01 requires implementing a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism. Let me understand the requirements:\n\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. Accept a call if: `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return `accepted_call_ids` and `diagnostics` in call order\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture case:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: loss_without=1.48911432, loss_with=0.30132987, tokens=5, parseable=true\n  - gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445\n  - normalized_gain = 1.18778445 / 5 = 0.23755689\n  - parseable=true, normalized_gain \u003e= 0.05 → accepted\n- call1: 1.37006381 - 0.10127803 = 1.26878578 / 5 = 0.25375716 → accepted\n- call2: 1.07992348 - 0.04054692 = 1.03937656 / 5 = 0.20787531 → accepted\n- call3: 1.76582941 - 0.57732788 = 1.18850153 / 3 = 0.39616718 → accepted\n- call4: 1.70674574 - 0.40289862 = 1.30384712 / 6 = 0.21730785 → accepted\n- call5: 1.98682122 - 0.89260518 = 1.09421604 / 4 = 0.27355401, parseable=false → rejected\n\nThe output format requires `normalized_gain` to be rounded. How many decimal places? The problem says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but doesn't specify. Let me check if rounding affects acceptance decisions. The threshold is 0.05, so I'll use a reasonable rounding like round to some number of decimal places. The problem says \"rounded\" but doesn't specify how many... I'll use round() with perhaps 8 decimal places, or just return the float directly. Actually looking at the schema, it says `\"type\": \"number\"` so just a float. I'll round to a reasonable precision, maybe not at all, or maybe use `round(val, 10)` to keep it clean.\n\nWait, re-reading: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" This means the diagnostics values should be rounded. Without a specific precision, I'll round to a sensible number like 8 decimal places.\n\nActually, let me just implement it simply:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 10),\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThe candidate artifact mentions:\n- `normalized_weights` - might mean weighted by token count? But I think the normalization is simply `gain / tokens`\n- `stronger_counterfactual` - this means we use `loss_without - loss_with` (the stronger counterfactual is: what would the model predict without this call)\n- `inclusive_threshold` - means `\u003e=` not `\u003e`\n- `stable_order` - preserve source order in diagnostics\n\nAll of these seem consistent with my implementation. Let me also add validation for required fields.\n\nThe schema also says `raise ValueError for infeasible or structurally invalid case`. Let me add validation.\n\nFor rounding, I'll use `round(normalized_gain, 10)` to avoid floating point noise but this might be overkill. Let me just not round at all since Python floats are already fine, or use a minimal rounding. Actually the problem says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" so I should round. I'll use 8 decimal places as a reasonable precision.\n\nWait, actually re-reading: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" I think this might mean the diagnostics list should be returned in call order (which I'm doing), and \"rounded\" might refer to the values being reasonable floats. I'll round to 8 places to be safe.\n\nLet me write the final implementation:\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: calls\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be numeric\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        for field in (\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"):\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required field '{field}' in call\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(tokens, (int, float)) or tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain_rounded \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain_rounded,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01HEl6QkUIEc2AyP4UbYLQRU","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2434},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2434,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":78,"output_tokens":1721,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1217},"service_tier":"standard"}}